window.docContents[155].resolve({"/Elementary-Functions/___4___37-Inverse-Hyperbolic-Functions/#LMLF-___-DLMF-with-Lean--Elementary-Functions--___4___37-Inverse-Hyperbolic-Functions--___4___37-Inverse-Hyperbolic-Functions--Fundamental-property":{"contents":"Source: DLMF §4.37(v)\n\nE26–E28 are the equations z=sinh w, z=cosh w, and z=tanh w; the Lean\ndisclosures record their direct implication to the corresponding inverse-value\nsets. E29–E31 now characterize all inverse values using k∈ℤ and the\ndisplayed sign families.\n\n\n\n","context":"LMLF · DLMF with Lean\u0009Elementary Functions\u0009§4.37 Inverse Hyperbolic Functions\u0009§4.37 Inverse Hyperbolic Functions","header":"Fundamental property","id":"/Elementary-Functions/___4___37-Inverse-Hyperbolic-Functions/#LMLF-___-DLMF-with-Lean--Elementary-Functions--___4___37-Inverse-Hyperbolic-Functions--___4___37-Inverse-Hyperbolic-Functions--Fundamental-property"},"/Elementary-Functions/___4___4-Special-Values-and-Limits/#LMLF-___-DLMF-with-Lean--Elementary-Functions--___4___4-Special-Values-and-Limits--___4___4_LPAR_i_RPAR_-Logarithms":{"contents":"\\ln 1=0.The principal logarithm at one is zero.\n\n\\ln(-1\\mathbin{\\pm}i0)=\\mathbin{\\pm}\\pi i.Approaching the negative real axis from above or below gives the two boundary\nvalues of the principal logarithm, with arguments +π and −π.\n\n\\ln(\\mathord{\\pm}i)=\\mathord{\\pm}\\tfrac12\\pi i.The principal logarithm of the positive and negative imaginary units has\nargument ±π/2.\n\n","context":"LMLF · DLMF with Lean\u0009Elementary Functions\u0009§4.4 Special Values and Limits","header":"§4.4(i) Logarithms","id":"/Elementary-Functions/___4___4-Special-Values-and-Limits/#LMLF-___-DLMF-with-Lean--Elementary-Functions--___4___4-Special-Values-and-Limits--___4___4_LPAR_i_RPAR_-Logarithms"}});